module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_constructor_asserts_a_provenance_its_value_does_not_have

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data a_constructor_asserts_a_provenance_its_value_does_not_have: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_constructor_asserts_a_provenance_its_value_does_not_have" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "A COPRODUCT WHOSE ARMS NAME WHERE A NUMBER CAME FROM IS A PROVENANCE CLAIM, AND AN ARM CHOSEN BECAUSE NO OTHER ARM FITS IS A FALSE ONE. The invalid state is a value sitting under a constructor that says somebody MEASURED it when the measurement was of a different subject -- and unlike a wrong number, it cannot be caught by checking the number, because the number may be perfectly correct for the thing that was actually measured.",
    "THE INSTANCE, 2026-09-11: gunbc.spark.pair_serving_desired spark_pair_serving_seq_capacity is SeqCapacityMeasured { max_num_seqs: 32 }, and 32 was genuinely read off a vLLM launch line. What it is USED for is the argument a future pair-serving convergence would launch with; what its constructor says is that a running engine reported it. Those became different subjects the moment the route stopped serving: the DeepSeek answering on the head's front door was launched out of band from a container that has since exited, so no running engine on that route has ever been read. The type's three arms -- measured, operator policy, unmeasured -- partition by WHO CHOSE the number, and the row landed under the one that says an engine reported it.",
    "WHERE THE HONEST HOME IS, STATED AS OPEN RATHER THAN SETTLED, because this row's first spelling asserted an answer and another lane found a better one within the hour. I wrote that a launch argument has no arm of its own, so the type needed a fourth partitioned by subject. The competing reading is that copying `--max-num-seqs` off an argv IS A CHOICE and not evidence, so the operator-policy arm is already its home, and the measured arm should mean an engine observed INDEPENDENTLY of the argv it was asked to launch with -- pool standing, scheduler occupancy -- rather than a re-read of what we told it to do. That reading is stronger: it needs no new arm and no new observation, and it sharpens what `Measured` means instead of adding a neighbour beside it. It is being settled in its own change. What is NOT in question either way, and is what this row records, is that the value sat under a constructor asserting a provenance it did not have.",
    "WHY IT IS NOT REPAIRED BY REFUSING, WHICH IS THE FIRST THING A READER WILL PROPOSE. Answering SeqCapacityUnmeasured there has been tried and it DEADLOCKED THE FLEET: the unit refuses, so the realization refuses, so the apply plan refuses, so no engine starts -- and the launch line that would supply a measurement can only come from an engine that started. A wall with no path through it is not the highest honest rung; it is a refusal that prevents the evidence which would retire it (manager ruling, 2026-09-11).",
    "WHAT DISCHARGED THE SAFETY HALF, so the residue is scoped honestly. gunbc.serving.serving_enrollment declines to inherit this number: a route's admission ceiling is CeilingByDeclaredPolicy or CeilingFromRouteLaunch, and neither reads it. Nothing that admits a turn consumes the overclaiming row any more, which turns it from a fail-open into a documentation defect -- real, ranked, and not worth deadlocking a fleet to close.",
    "THE REPAIR, AND WHAT I GOT WRONG ABOUT ITS COST. I judged the repair to require the running-engine reading that gunbc.rung_drop.harness_seat_ceiling_by_operator_policy names as its restoration, and therefore to be blocked until that receipt exists. That was wrong, and wrong in the expensive direction: under the reading above the repair is a RECLASSIFICATION -- move the value to the arm that already describes it -- which needs no observation at all, is deadlock-safe because only the unmeasured arm refuses, and could have been done immediately. Mistaking a naming repair for one that waits on evidence is its own small failure, and it is recorded here because the shape recurs: a defect whose honest fix is free reads as blocked when its author has a costlier fix in mind. The structural cut one layer up -- gunbc.serving.serving_enrollment ServingRouteTurnCeiling splitting CeilingByDeclaredPolicy from CeilingFromRouteLaunch -- remains the model for where such a distinction lives.",
    "THE SIBLING CLASS, AND WHY THESE ARE TWO ROWS RATHER THAN ONE. gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_constant_enforces_a_law_narrower_than_its_own_annotation is the same coarseness seen from the other side: there the PROSE is honest and the carrier enforces something wider than it says; here the prose was silent and the CONSTRUCTOR claims something the value does not know. A reader asking 'why is my guard over-applying' and a reader asking 'why does this type say measured' are hunting different things, so the rows are kept apart and cite each other. Both were found in one lane on one day, which is the tell that the shared root -- a carrier too coarse for the distinction its author needed, resolved by overclaiming instead of by widening the carrier -- is worth watching for directly.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
